sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant Proxy as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS<br/>TLS 1.2+
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API Server<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Upstream as Upstream Service<br/>8080/TCP HTTP<br/>(localhost)

    Note over Client,Upstream: Flow 1: Authenticated Request Proxy

    Client->>Proxy: HTTPS Request (port 8443)<br/>Auth: Bearer Token (OIDC or SA token)
    Proxy->>Proxy: Check WithAllowPaths<br/>(bypass if path matches)

    alt Path NOT in allow-list
        Proxy->>K8sAPI: TokenReview (HTTPS 6443)<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token
        K8sAPI-->>Proxy: TokenReview Response<br/>(authenticated user info)

        Proxy->>K8sAPI: SubjectAccessReview (HTTPS 6443)<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token
        K8sAPI-->>Proxy: SubjectAccessReview Response<br/>(allowed/denied)

        alt Authorized
            Proxy->>Proxy: WithAuthHeaders<br/>(inject identity headers)
            Proxy->>Upstream: HTTP Request (port 8080)<br/>+ X-Remote-User, X-Remote-Groups
            Upstream-->>Proxy: HTTP Response
            Proxy-->>Client: HTTPS Response
        else Denied
            Proxy-->>Client: 403 Forbidden
        end
    else Path in allow-list (e.g., /healthz)
        Proxy->>Upstream: HTTP Request (port 8080)<br/>No auth check
        Upstream-->>Proxy: HTTP Response
        Proxy-->>Client: HTTPS Response
    end

    Note over Client,Upstream: Flow 2: Health Check (Bypass)

    participant Probe as Liveness/Readiness<br/>Probe

    Probe->>Proxy: HTTPS /healthz<br/>(proxyEndpoints listener)<br/>No auth required
    Proxy-->>Probe: 200 OK "ok"
